 "_note": "F94 eliminated the MEAN of single-token sensitivity as the explanandum for lambda_ca. Annealed mean field uses only that mean; this measures the two things it discards -- the across-context spread (masking / canalization) and the departure of the two-flip response from independence (cancellation) -- on the same three-rung ladder, in three context regimes including the settled ring the dynamics actually run in. The (spread, subadd) pair is needed because XOR and majority are both sub-additive for opposite structural reasons; DK's p2=0 line and ECA rule 150 are the cancellation anchors, rule 232 the masking anchor, and separating them is a registered gate on reading rung 3 at all."
